  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo></math> The highest prime factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>.</p><p>Since, the only prime factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Also, factors of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Out of these, the highest prime factor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Similarly the highest prime factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>128</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So, the given function is many one.</p><p>Now, no composite number will be image of any number.</p><p>Example: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> is not image of any element</p><p>So, the given function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is into.</p><p>Hence many one and into</p><p>Or, neither one-one nor onto.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
